  "final_answer": "**Cause:** `suggestions.ts` called `POST /api/recommend`, but the backend only serves `POST /api/colleges/recommend`. That route is defined in `python-backend/api/routes.py` and mounted under `/api`. Nothing was registered at `/api/recommend`, so every call got a 404.\n\nThe request body was also wrong. The backend's `RecommendRequest` requires a `student_profile` object. The client was sending `{student_id, answers}` at the top level. Fixing only the URL would have turned the 404 into a 422.\n\n**Fix:** I changed both recommendation calls in `suggestions.ts`, in `generateSuggestedColleges` and `generateSuggestedCollegesFromAnswers`:\n- The URL is now `/api/colleges/recommend`.\n- The body is now `{ student_profile: { student_id, answers } }`.\n\nI made no backend change and added no alias route, so the backend still has a single recommendation endpoint. The other client callers (`useCollegeListGenerator.ts` and `collegeApi.ts`) already used the correct path.\n\n`run_tests` now passes. It only reads the files as text, so I haven't tested against a running backend.\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `client/src/services/college/suggestions.ts`",
